# oracle: the pressure of pair hybrid granular surf/granular: w154gs_screw_hertz (in.screwfeeder.local cut down to the helix STL, 7 poured spheres, hertz, 85 steps, first contact at step ~55) with press and its components. As in native, pair granular tallies its virial contact by contact, so surf/granular in the hybrid does too, from the contact point
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 7.9e-8, atoms 2.9e-9. The thermo figure is pyy at step 60 (2.4e-5 beside pzz 1.1e-3), trajectory round-off as ke's 1.4e-9; before the fix press differed by 2.2e-5 at step 60.
# oracle-inputs: w151gs_surf.helix.stl
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 atomrel=1e-8
units           lj
atom_style      hybrid tri sphere 1
atom_modify     map array
boundary        f f f
dimension       3
comm_modify     vel yes cutoff 1.0
region          box block -2 2 -2 16 -2 7 units box
create_box      3 box
fix             1 all surface/local input stl 3 2 w151gs_surf.helix.stl flat 10.0
pair_style      hybrid granular surf/granular
pair_coeff      1 * surf/granular hertz 1.0 1.0 tangential linear_history 0.0 0.0 0.0
pair_coeff      1 1 granular hertz 1.0 1.0 tangential linear_history 0.0 0.0 0.0
pair_coeff      2*3 2*3 none
region          insert_region cylinder z 0 12 1.6 3 5 side in units box
group           sphere type 1
group           corkscrew molecule 2
fix             2 sphere nve/sphere
fix             3 sphere gravity 0.1 vector 0 0 -1
fix             4 sphere pour 7 1 7892374 region insert_region diam range 0.5 1.0
compute         1 all ke
timestep        0.05
thermo          5
thermo_style    custom step ke atoms c_1 press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g lost ignore
fix             5 corkscrew move rotate 0 0 0 0 1 0 1000 units box
run             85
